Hi Christine,

Thank you for taking the time to walk through the overnight examples today. I=
'm glad you can take the materials back for the handoff explanation.

The two Detroit windows are both Friday, 06:00=E2=80=9307:00 EST, but they ar=
e different Fridays: R-611 leaves Chicago on December 5 and has its Detroit w=
indow on December 6; R-614 leaves Chicago on December 12 and has its Detroit =
window on December 13. Saying the local date at each end makes the distinctio=
n clear. For R-615, the Indianapolis window opens December 12 at 23:30 and cl=
oses December 13 at 00:30 EST, so the closing date needs to be named too.

I've attached the slides we discussed and the one-page reading-order referenc=
e with the English and Japanese examples. The six planned examples contain no=
 actual arrival times, so they cannot be used to estimate the number of actua=
l late deliveries.

Best,
Jennifer

